Back in August I created a new interface for the Windows version of
NetHack. In appearance it resembles the Windows version of RevivedHack
1.4/1.5. It's still in its early stages of development, but works well
enough for what it does. Here are some of its features:

* The interface looks similar to the Windows console version, but has
two different font sizes (one for the dungeon, the other for messages),
brighter colors, and graphical effects not possible in the console
version (no effects have yet been implemented in this release)

* A window menu that contains most NetHack commands

* Mouse movement

* A screenshot can be saved with the F11 key

* Fullscreen mode (640x480) can be toggled on/off with the F12 key

The interface comes in the form of a source code patch (no original
files are overwritten). The source code and a NetHack 3.43 binary can
be downloaded from its SourceForge project page:
http://sourceforge.net/projects/nh-hyb-interf/


